meru, m. N. of a fabulous golden mountain 🞄in the centre of Jambudvīpa, round 🞄which the planets are supposed to revolve;
 🞄central bead of a rosary;
 joints protruding 🞄in certain positions of the fingers: -kūṭa, 🞄m. or n. summit of Meru;
 -dhāman, a. having 🞄his abode on Mount Meru;
 -dhvaja, m. 🞄N. of a prince;
 -yantra, n. spindle;
 -vardhana, m. N..
